					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5156</guid>
				<title>Ignorer</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5156</link>
				<description>

&lt;p&gt;Item #: SCP-5156&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/furball349&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7165363&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1608972647&quot; alt=&quot;furball349&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7165363)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/furball349&quot;  &gt;furball349&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
				<pubDate>Sat, 26 Dec 2020 08:43:54 +0000</pubDate>
												<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Item #: SCP-5156</p> <p>Object Class: Euclid</p> <p>Special Containment procedures: SCP-5156 need to be contained in a locked room dimensions of 10 and 9 feet except for testing procedures. Clearance of level 4 personnel may enter it's containment.</p> <p>Description: SCP-5156 is a humanoid scp which has power of getting ignored especially for scp's. This effect doesn't seem to work on humans. The SCP foundation get to know it's power on a cleaning session of SCP-173's containment</p> <p>Origin: On a cleaning session of SCP-173's Containment SCP-5156 entered along with another two D-Class personnel. Unfortunately the power went out the researchers heard two crunching of necks.<br /> The personnel managed to get power back on they see SCP-5156 crouching in fear as SCP-173 starred at it. The researchers were shocked to see this as SCP-5156 was asked to come out</p> <p>Addendum: As the incident has shocked the researchers but also it made them curious to see what happens if they tested it with other scp's. This SCP handled by Dr.Rivian he is an unstoppable researchers if he started nothing can stop him.<br /> This not only it's power it's true power revealed at SCP-173's Containment breach. Dr.Martha a female researcher who worked near SCP-173's Containment.<br /> That day the gates of SCP-173's chamber opened SCP-173 moves towards the Dr but suddenly SCP-5156 appeared and attacked SCP-173 by grabbing it's throat and throwing it down</p> <p>Experiment Log 1: Dr.Rivian decided to test it with SCP-054 The little girl SCP-5156 stepped into the little girl's the door behind we're closed Dr.Rivian Curiously waiting. After ten minutes a MTF guard open's the door and asked SCP-5156 to come out.<br /> Dr.Rivian asked SCP-5156 &quot;How do feel in there&quot;<br /> SCP-5156 replied &quot;Nothing special at first she look little scared but next she asked me to read a book&quot;<br /> Dr.Rivian take note of it ordered MTF guards to take it back to it's containment</p> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/furball349" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7165363&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608972647" alt="furball349" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7165363)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/furball349" >furball349</a></span></p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5673</guid>
				<title>SCP-5673</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5673</link>
				<description>

&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: right;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Item #:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5673
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Object Class:&lt;/strong&gt; Safe&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Containment Procedures:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5673 is to be contained in a sealed glass cover on a pedestal 42 inches in height, If the object is not contained 42 inches off the ground it will shake violently and will admit ionizing radiation until placed on any surface that is 42 inches specifically in height.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5673 is an indestructible black pen with no visible brand name given on the object. SCP-5673 has the strange ability to grant any wish written on any type of paper as long as the wish is not malicious or will cause harm to a living being the wish will be granted. If a wish is malicious or harmful to a living being, the pen user&#039;s blood will start to turn to ink, and their bones might snap but this isn&#039;t guaranteed. It was also found that the anomalous ink from SCP-5673 mixes with 50% of the users&#039; blood when the user writes their wish on paper.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Addendum 5673-01:&lt;/strong&gt; A D-Class is instructed to write his wish with SCP-5673 on the paper in front of him. A few seconds pass as the D-Class writes &amp;quot;A piece of chocolate cake&amp;quot; on the paper, After one minute the desired object appears on the table in front of the subject. The subject was told that they could not keep the cake and was escorted out of the room. The piece of chocolate cake was tested for anomalous properties, none were found.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Addendum 5673-02:&lt;/strong&gt; A D-Class is instructed to write his wish with SCP-5673 on the paper in front of him. A few seconds pass as the D-Class writes &amp;quot;The death of ███████&amp;quot; on the paper, After one minute the D-Class starts to look visibly ill by their blood being turned into ink and their body starts to twist and break until the subject&#039;s death.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Addendum 5673-03:&lt;/strong&gt; A D-Class is instructed to write &amp;quot;The destruction of SCP-173&amp;quot; on the paper in front of him. After one minute the D-Class starts to look visibly ill by their blood being turned into ink.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ghostghpm&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4894680&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1608972647&quot; alt=&quot;GhostGHPM&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4894680)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ghostghpm&quot;  &gt;GhostGHPM&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 25 Dec 2020 19:22:54 +0000</pubDate>
												<content:encoded>
