					<![CDATA[
						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-4273</p> <p><strong>Object Class:</strong> <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Safe</span> Euclid</p> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> SCP-4273 is to be kept at Site-95, in a standard size anomalous vehicle containment bay with all surfaces covered in blast-resistant plating.</p> <p>Every 6-7 months SCP-4273 is to be checked for maintenance issues. Should there be issues with any of its components, they are to be fixed as soon as possible to avoid any risk of SCP-4273 becoming unstable. Under no circumstances is SCP-4273 to be allowed to <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">activate its weaponry</span> be activated unless in a controlled and prepared testing environment approved by site command.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-800907-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup></p> <p>Should SCP-4273 endure massive amounts of physical damage during testing or field use, it is to be put in between Tesla coils approved by Level-3 engineers until its self-repair protocol is complete. <span style="color: blue">In accordance with Event-4273-4-CB, every 25th of December SCP-4273 is to be immediatly incapacitated via the C4 package in the middle of the chamber. SCP-4273 will be allowed to activate repair protocols after the 27th of December, and the C4 package replaced.</span></p> <p>Should SCP-4273 enter an unstable state as indicated by the sudden rapid vibration of SCP-4273, the blast doors leading to the entrance of its containment bay are to be closed immediately. The blast doors are to be kept closed for approximately thirty to forty minutes until all signs of the anomalous heat cease, at which point cleanup and maintenance is to commence. SCP-4273 is to be handled with caution for the next 24 hours after said event.</p> <p>SCP-4273-1 is currently kept in a standard anomaly locker. SCP-4273-1 is only to be used in testing and field usage by personnel with the requirements for a bonding procedure. Personnel are to rotate shifts to avoid a potential containment breach.</p> <p>In the event that any SCP-4273 instance is encountered outside of containment, MTF-Epsilon-212 “Dragon Riders” is to be immediately dispatched to contain or terminate the instance, depending on the current situation. <span style="color: blue">In accordance with Event-4273-4-CB, MTF-Epsilon-212 is to report to site-95 as a precaution.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-800907-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >2</a></sup></span></p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-4273 is a black Mack Titan semi-truck, weighing approximately 125 tonnes. SCP-4273 has been observed accelerating towards 240&#160;km/h within 2 seconds, despite not facilitating the engine power necessary to achieve said speeds[<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-800907-3" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >3</a></sup> This has also allowed SCP-4273X to be extremely resistant to physical damage, as several tests and incidents have shown SCP-4273 being left as rusted and crumpled, yet completely immune to further harm of the SCP. See <strong>Addendum:Event-4273-4-CB</strong> for more details.</p> <p>SCP-4273 is shown to have a self-repair protocol, which is only observed when SCP-4273 is exposed to any source of electricity with high voltage. The exact method of this protocol's activation is unknown, but the hood of SCP-4273 will open, and a pair of conjoined jumper cables attached to any source of electricity. If the source is out of reach, the cables will act as a conductor, causing the source to emit an unknown form of energy that has been described as “Pure electricity”, although the exact nature of this energy has yet to be studied extensively due to the longevity of the protocol.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-800907-4" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >4</a></sup></p> <p>SCP-4273’s <span style="color: blue">former</span> most notable property, however, is the vast amount of weaponry and components stored in different areas of SCP-4273’s body, as most should not be able to fit inside of SCP-4273 due to the size of several of the weapons.</p> <p>A list of these weapons and components with locations and activation methods has been documented.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>NOTE:</strong> Personnel assigned to SCP-4273 that attempt or request any further attempts into studying and understanding SCP-4273 are required to view the list to become familiar with the components. Personnel not assigned to SCP-4273 are not required to view the list.</p> </blockquote> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;View&nbsp;armaments</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;hide&nbsp;armaments&nbsp;</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <blockquote> <p><span style="font-size:0.8em;">Yes we are indeed aware that this list is rather pointless. No, we will not remove it as the latest breach has led to the creation of this list so we may be better prepared for a potential containment breach. -Dr. Sparks</span></p> </blockquote> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>Weapon/Component identification</th> <th>Location</th> <th>Mode of activation</th> <th>Additional notes</th> </tr> <tr> <td>2 Breda-SAFATs</td> <td>Hidden in the front fenders having a visible belt with HEAT type ammunition.</td> <td>Two buttons on the sides of the steering wheel.</td> <td>All attempts of removing the belt from the side of the gun have proved fruitless.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Quad barrel ZPU</td> <td>Hidden within the roof of SCP-4273.</td> <td>A switch located on the dashboard.</td> <td>While it has no visible ammunition, it fires what appears to be HEAT type bullets, capable of penetrating most metals and exploding upon contact.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Various Mines</td> <td>License plate on the rear bumpers and the fifth wheel.</td> <td>A series of buttons under the wheel.</td> <td>L9 Bar Mines, heavily modified naval mines, a variety of land mines, and an uncategorized explosive capable of showering shrapnel in a 2-meter radius have been observed being dispensed.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>M6 Flame Gun</td> <td>Stored within the front grille mesh of the SCP.</td> <td>A switch located inside of the stick shift, and a grip button on the wheel.</td> <td>Flames are capable of reaching ████° C.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Pilots</td> <td>Guarding the wheels front bumper of SCP-4273.</td> <td>N/A</td> <td>Serving as a protection to both, as attempts at removing them have failed. They are also seen acting as brakes when SCP-4273 exceeds 120&#160;km/h.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Chain grapple</td> <td>Stored in the front license plate.</td> <td>A small push button in front of the gas pedal.</td> <td>Capable of reaching 7.62m in length. It can pull at least 40 tons, in a matter of seconds.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Barbed and razor wire</td> <td>Located on the roof, as well as the front and rear bumpers.</td> <td>N/A</td> <td>They do not appear to have any anomalous effects other than being unbreakable.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Modified V8 engine</td> <td>Front of the SCP</td> <td>N/A</td> <td>Several personnel have claimed that the engine contains 8000 pistons. How or why these claims have been made is unknown, as the only modification visible on the engine is the connection made to the M6 flame gun.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Tinted bullet-resistant glass</td> <td>Doors and windshield</td> <td>N/A</td> <td>N/A</td> </tr> <tr> <td>[DATA EXPUNGED]</td> <td>Underneath a pre-installed bobblehead.</td> <td>A small button located in the bobblehead.</td> <td>Responsible for the destruction of testing Site 12.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Various unknown components</td> <td>Various areas</td> <td>N/A</td> <td>Several standard vehicle components such as the gas tank, speedometer, and even the rearview mirror are completely disconnected, non-functional, and even completely removed, testing ongoing.</td> </tr> </table> </div> </div> </div> <p><span style="color: blue">SCP-4273 is Autonomous to an unknown degree. SCP-4273 mainly will display minor signs of self imposed movement, such as rotating to face the entrance to it’s containment chamber. On the 25th of December, SCP will instead activate automatically. As of Event-4273-4-CB, all activations have shown the same behavior. SCP-4273 will attempt to cause intense damage to the area it is currently located in. Interestingly, SCP-4273 will avoid harming anything related to Christmas.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-800907-5" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >5</a></sup></span></p> <p>The vehicle’s ignition key, designated as SCP-4273-1 is constructed in a highly unusual fashion. It is currently the only object that activates both its engine, and its weapons, and is considered the most valuable component of SCP-4273.</p> <p>SCP-4273-1 can only be used by personnel who meet specific requirements.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-800907-6" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >6</a></sup> Any other personnel who attempt to use SCP-4273-1 to start SCP-4273 will not cause any effect other than SCP-4273 to refuse to start. However, it should be noted that if this is continuously tried for more than 5 attempts, SCP-4273 will enter a destabilization state, at which point the engine will proceed to emit highly lethal amounts of carbon monoxide in a thick cloud, covering at least 2 miles in diameter in less than 2 minutes before igniting, killing any life form within its presence.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-800907-7" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >7</a></sup></p> <p>SCP-4273-2 refers to any trailer attached to SCP-4273. Trailers will gain anomalous properties once attached to SCP-4273, all having varying properties depending on the attachment, yet some have been found to have constant properties, namely the growth of barbed and razor wire along any edges on the outside of the vehicle.</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Attempts to find any potential individuals responsible for SCP-4273 are underway.</span><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-800907-8" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >8</a></sup></p> <p><strong>Addendum:</strong> Recovery log and After-Incident-Report-4273-RC<br /> SCP-4273 was recovered from a small town in El Paso, Texas, where a local demolition derby was being held. Doctor Sparks, who was on vacation at the time, witnessed SCP-4273’s effects when an attack by local drug cartels attempted to storm the area, presumably to kill several workers seeing as how later investigation revealed drug usage, though SCP-4273 was used to successfully terminate all attackers. However, the driver and previous possessor of SCP-4273-1 was fatally shot during the event. Dr. Sparks attempted to aid the driver, who instructed them to take SCP-4273 and let it run free before expiring. SCP-4273 was secured and contained, and the remaining survivors were given Class C amnestics. See after-incident-report for more information.</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;interview&nbsp;log</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Collapse&nbsp;interview&nbsp;log</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <blockquote> <p><strong>Interviewed:</strong>Subject-█ a survivor of the incident, the manager of the event.</p> <p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> Doctor Sparks</p> <p><strong>Foreword:</strong>Interrogation of Subject-█ after recovery of SCP-4273.</p> <p><strong>&lt;Begin Log&gt;</strong></p> <p><strong>Doctor Sparks:</strong> Are you aware of why you are here?</p> <p><strong>Subject-█:</strong> Not exactly, but if I had to take a guess, I’d say it's because of what happened earlier?</p> <p><strong>Doctor Sparks:</strong> Where Was the truck found exactly?</p> <p><strong>Subject-█:</strong> You mean the Titan?</p> <p><strong>Doctor Sparks:</strong> Yes, do you know how it got there?</p> <p><strong>Subject-█:</strong> I don’t know man, it just showed up, key and all.</p> <p><strong>Doctor Sparks:</strong> You mean to say that SCP-4273 just showed up out of thin air?</p> <p><strong>Subject-█:</strong> I mean, kind of. It just showed up one day, we tried it out and next thing we knew, we had a new attraction for the show, I mean we weren't about to let this pass up. You don’t just get a gift and question where it came from. Plus, a few months ago, we were running low on cash.<br /> <strong>Doctor Sparks:</strong> You mean you all could operate SCP-4273 without any trouble?</p> <p><strong>Subject-█:</strong> Technically no. Seeing how big a hippy ███ was, it just wouldn’t start, even when he tried to hotwire it. Heck, when ███████ decided to become a medical doctor, the truck wouldn't start until he got drunk and even then it seemed to stop sometimes like he was trying to fight back against his inner rage.</p> <p><strong>Doctor Sparks:</strong> You mean to tell me that SCP-4273 will not respond to anyone with good intentions?</p> <p><strong>Subject-█:</strong> Two things. One, terrible nickname for it, just wanted to point that out. Two, actually no, it just worked for any one of us who just liked to live a little, have an adrenaline rush, enjoy high octane action, that kind of stuff. Look, basically as long as we didn't give a crap for our safety or others, we could drive it no problem<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-800907-9" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >9</a></sup> Or at least that's how I was told why the thing wouldn't budge when I tried to drive it. I've driven some of the most complex things with no sweat, but this just caused my head to spin. That or it didn’t like me. Either way, I guess that's how ██████ was able to drive that thing with no problem.</p> <p><strong>Doctor Sparks:</strong> I see. Was the attack by that gang-related to SCP-4273 in any way?</p> <p><strong>Subject-█:</strong> Not really, I mean one of them did notice it and tried to get in before ██████ knocked ‘em out and got in and just annihilated them! Funny thing is, she was supposed to go up next for her performance with<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-800907-10" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >10</a></sup>, as you call it,spc-4372?</p> <p><strong>Doctor Sparks:</strong>Close. While we also found that you had several workers who were in touch with the gang, are you sure no other motives were the cause for the attack? Like a rivalry or territory violation?</p> <p><strong>Subject-█:</strong>No, I told them to get sober, obviously they didn’t, had to pay a huge debt, decided to give our tour a bad name, trashed everything, and now we're here. Honestly, this is the second biggest mishap we have had in the derby's history. Now can I please go? You know, I still have this thing to run. We’re putting on a christmas special soon, and it’s gonna be the big reveal!</p> <p><strong>&lt;End Log&gt;</strong></p> <p><strong>Closing Statement:</strong> After the events of the interview, Subject was given class-c amnestics, and investigation of the location the event was held at, several narcotics were found, as well as a contact list related to the cartel involved in the incident, along with a schedule list, and plans for upcoming events, most of which were to involve SCP-4273.</p> </blockquote> <p>Shortly after the initial containment of SCP-4273, a small torn business card was found in the glove compartment of SCP-4273, with text reading “Renex Industries”<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-800907-11" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >11</a></sup> <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Current speculation suggests that SCP-4273 is a product of this company, but no evidence has been found, other than the card itself, about this organization's existence</span><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-800907-12" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >12</a></sup></p> </div> </div> </div> <p><strong>Addendum-4273-T2:</strong> The following is a partial log detailing tests conducted on SCP-4273 to find any additional anomalous properties should a trailer be attached. The tests shown are the most noticeable in changes in trailer properties and appearances, as most are repetitive and do not seem to change other than the growth of barbed and razor wire on the sides of the trailers.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-800907-13" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >13</a></sup></p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;testing&nbsp;log</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Collapse&nbsp;testing&nbsp;log</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Test C</strong>- Date██/██/██</span></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Subject:</strong> SCP-4273, one tank trailer, primarily used for transporting gasoline.</p> <p><strong>Procedure:</strong> The Trailer car was successfully attached to SCP-4273 without incident. The tank was loaded with gasoline beforehand.</p> <p><strong>Results:</strong> <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">No noticeable differences other than barbed wire “growths”</span> the entire holding tank was composed of several layers of Lead, Titanium, and Cobalt, all of which are not used in such vehicles. Its weight remained the same. The gasoline appeared to be mildly corrosive.</p> <p><strong>Notes:</strong> It appears that SCP-4273 changed the trailer to either hold a more aggressive substance or to withstand potential damage dealt in case of an emergency. This may be useful if SCP-4273 is approved for field use, as there are quite a few hostile substances we've encountered over the years.-Sparks</p> </blockquote> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Test J</strong>- Date██/██/██</span></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Subject:</strong> SCP-4273, one field artillery cannon.<br /> <strong>Procedure:</strong> The field artillery cannon was attached to the truck after security personnel were able to goad D-2001 into operating SCP-4273. The artillery cannon was not armed.<br /> <strong>Results:</strong> The artillery cannon displayed signs of sentiance, and attempted to move and drag SCP-4273 as it headed towards the exit area of testing zone-23. The artillery cannon was capable of producing a variety of sounds, metallic and equine in nature. The cannon fired three rounds before being detached from SCP-4273, where it ceased all movement.<br /> <strong>Notes:</strong> Because of this event, all trailer attachments involving weapons or objects that could be used as weapons are prohibited from testing until more information about SCP-4273 can be found.</p> </blockquote> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Test K</strong>- Date██/██/██</span></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Subject:</strong> SCP-4273, one horse trailer<br /> <strong>Procedure:</strong> The Trailer car was successfully attached to SCP-4273 without incident. A domestic horse was loaded into the trailer beforehand.</p> <p><strong>Results:</strong> After about 5 seconds after being attached, the trailer started shaking violently. Upon opening the doors, an unusually large wild horse<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-800907-14" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >14</a></sup>, resembling the domestic horse from before, ran out and bit several agents while bucking frantically. It was eventually sedated via injection from 3 horse tranquilizers. The subject was eventually released into the wild after confirmation that the horse did not show any other signs of anomalous properties and was deemed safe for release.</p> <p><strong>Notes:</strong> Along with the recent information gathered by several Task forces, this proves that SCP-4273 is indeed meant for use in combat scenarios or other such uses, as the horse was not for racing. I currently advise that usage of SCP-4273 be handled with proper care if it is granted usage.-Sparks</p> </blockquote> </div> </div> </div> <p><strong>Addendum 4273-A-R/R:</strong> Attempted raid and recovery.</p> <p>On ██/██/████, several Foundation investigative personnel had reported a warehouse that was discovered to have been holding more than 66 instances of SCP-4273, almost all of which were in severe condition by a group of urban explorers who had reported it to a local newspaper in [REDACTED]. Foundation agents embedded in the area were able to suppress the report before it could be properly published, with witnesses given Class-A amnestics. Agents were able to locate the warehouse as described by witnesses.</p> <p>Upon attempting to interact with and contain the SCP-4273 instances, all of the instances proceed to enter an unstable state and proceed to explode simultaneously. No remains were found afterward. During the event, one agent reported seeing an unusually large horse with red skin in the warehouse during the climax of the event. While an examination of the area did not report a body, a collection of documents was found within a blast resistant safe.</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;Recovered&nbsp;document</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;document</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <blockquote> <p>Congratulations on purchasing the <span style="text-decoration: underline;">_Defensive Assault Truck</span>_ from Renex Industries, Vehicle &amp; Transportation Division. However, you must sign to agree to the following conditions before we can allow you to own and use our product.<br /> By signing this document, you hereby:</p> <ul> <li>Accept full responsibility for any and all damage dealt to passengers, cargo, and self.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>Allow for this product to be used for its intended purpose only.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>Agree to not tamper with any components that change its main functions <ul> <li style="list-style: none; display: inline"> <ul> <li>Said functions being <span style="text-decoration: underline;">_To terminate hostiles during escort and transportation, or use in assaults or defenses against hostile forces.</span>_</li> </ul> </li> </ul> </li> </ul> <ul> <li>Accept full responsibility for the care and condition of this product, and accept responsibility for any injuries, dismemberment, death, and any kind of manipulation dealt to the body, mind and/or spirit.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>Agree to terms stating that Arnex Conveyance:V&amp;T, and Renex Industries as a whole is not liable for any of the above conditions being broken, ignored, altered, or contaminated.</li> </ul> <p>* If any of the terms above are broken, will agree to return the product or accept the product's self destruct function<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-800907-15" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >15</a></sup>.</p> <p>PURCHASER’S SIGNATURE<br /> <span style="text-decoration: underline;">_██████</span>___</p> <p>APPROVAL SIGNATURE</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">_████_<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-800907-16" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >16</a></sup></span></p> </blockquote> <p>Attempts to find the listed individuals are currently ongoing, as with attempts to find any other products or locations associated with the company.</p> </div> </div> </div> <p><strong>Addendum:</strong>Event-4273-4-CB<br /> On the 25th of December, ████, SCP-4273 proceeded to manually activate, emitting sounds resembling grinding metal. SCP-4273 proceeded to breach containment, killing 3 personnel and causing massive damage to the site at large<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-800907-17" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >17</a></sup> before exiting the main building, eventually leaving the entirety of site-95. Recovery teams eventually located SCP-4273 in a remote town, causing massive property damage as well as causing, at current estimates, thirty civilian casualties. Recontainment of SCP-4273 took 5 hours after it had breached containment.</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;incident&nbsp;timeline</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Collapse&nbsp;incident&nbsp;timeline</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <blockquote> <p>SCP-4273 enters [REDACTED]</p> <p>SCP-4273 process to come to a stop. It remains this way for 2 minutes,</p> <p>SCP-4273 proceeds to ram itself into a tall building, causing the structure to collapse on top of it. SCP-4273 does not seem to be affected in any way.</p> <p>local law enforcement proceeded to approach SCP-4273 and open fire on SCP-4273 once it turned to face them, showing no driver. SCP-4273 retaliates by opening fire. All of the officers were killed in the ensuing firefight.</p> <p>SCP-4273 continues to destroy major parts of [REDACTED], killing 5 more civilians.</p> <p>After demolishing several more buildings in the area, SCP-4273 proceeds to move to the center of [REDACTED], before SCP-4273 proceeds to violently skid to a halt, hitting several pedestrians. Said pedestrians were confirmed dead upon impact.SCP-4273 narrowly avoids hitting an inflatable santa.</p> <p>Containment teams proceeded to attempt to recontain SCP-4273. 15 agents were maimed during the initial recontainment. 2 Helicopters were dispatched to assist with recontainment. MTF-Pi-1 is dispatched to aid in containment.</p> <p>SCP-4273 proceeds to engage helicopters, eliminating both via the ZPU turret and M6 flamethrower. SCP-4273 appears to be extremely protective of the inflatable santa.</p> <p>SCP-4273 evades all containment attempts for the next 13 minutes until a random bullet hits the santa, causing it to slowly deflate.</p> <p>SCP-4273 ceases movement and all hostilities. At this point, MTF-Epsilon-212 arrives and attempts to use SCP-4273-1 to regain control of SCP-4273.</p> <p>SCP-4273’s hood ornament glows intensly, proceeds to accelerate and rams into the containment truck. SCP-4273 then attempts to escape. SCP-4273-1 is lost for five minutes.</p> <p>SCP-4273 rams into a blockade, causing Agent ██████ to break his spine, paralyzing him.</p> <p>Two tanks are deployed to combat SCP-4273. During this time SCP-4273-1 is retrieved by containment personnel and Agent ██████ is tasked with entering SCP-4273 and inserting SCP-4273-1 into the key slot.</p> <p>Upon arrival, SCP-4273 engages both tanks, destroying one of them before being bombarded by artillery. SCP-4273s main front guns and turret are destroyed while SCP-4273 suffers minor harm, having several dents and rust spots covering it, despite the bombardment.</p> <p>SCP-4273 proceeds to burn several buildings, before ramming itself into the other tank. Bloodstains are visible on the hood of SCP-4273.</p> <p>SCP-4273 proceeds to violently destry several other buildings except those displaying holiday themes. At this time an airstrike was ordered by MTF-Epsilon-212.</p> <p>Agent ███████ has climbed onto and jumped off of a small building directly onto SCP-4273. SCP-4273 Attempts to remove Agent ███████ by raming itself into several buildings. All remaining tanks and personnel were told to hold fire.</p> <p>Agent ███████ enters SCP-4273, while the SCP attempts to engage all other vehicles in sight. Due to quick thinking by MTF-Epsilon-212 by hastily decorating several vehicles and personnel, no weaponry was used.</p> <p>Agent ███████’s head hits the steering wheel after SCP-4273 rams into a non decorated tank, causing him to go unconscious.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-800907-18" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >18</a></sup> SCP-4273 proceeds to attempt to leave the area. Barricades were put in place to prevent any attempt at further escape.</p> <p>Agent ███████ recovers after a minute and hastily attempts to insert SCP-4273-1 into SCP-4273. Agent ███████ successfully inserts SCP-4273-1 into SCP-4273, subduing the SCP. Agent ███████ is successful in leaving SCP-4273 so it may be recontained. Agent ████ unintentionally forgets to call off the airstrike.</p> <p>The airstrike hits SCP-4273. Despite being hit with over [REDACTED], SCP-4273 remained operational, despite being heavily rusted, dented, and burned. Several of the weapons have been destroyed, rendering SCP-4273 defenceless. MTF-Epsilon-212 proceeds to load SCP-4273 into a vehicle loader.</p> <p>SCP-4273 has been successfully recontained. All and all witnesses were given class-B amnestics and MTF-Pi-1 succeeded in creating a cover story of a terrorist attack.</p> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p>Containment procedures have been revised to accommodate this behavior. While it is currently unknown why or even how SCP-4273 was able to operate without SCP-4273-1, We have speculated that SCP-4273 may possess some form of autonomy. However that would not explain its escape from the site, specifically built to contain large non sentient movable objects. I recommend we make preparations in the event this does happen again, possibly with modifications to its containment cell. We cannot afford another breach, as the amount of resources and repairs we had to make was well over our annual budget.</p> <p>-Sparks.</p> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p><strong>Note:</strong> After another attempted breach a year later, containment procedures have been revised to include this behavior. Further research into this behavior is pending.</p> </blockquote> </div> </div> </div> <p><strong>Addendum:</strong>After-Incident-Report-4273-CB/R</p> <p>RECOVERED INTELLEGENCE-4273-CB/R<br /> After this event, MTF-Epsilon-12 had uncovered a mass production facility in [REDACTED]. Although the facility was in a state of severe neglect, several documents were found detailing the usage and means of production SCP-4273 underwent. Additionally, an advertisement for SCP-4273 was found, dating as far back as 1950. <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">No explanation for the date, manufacturing, or even potential sales have been found to support the time of print however.</span> G.O.I-XXX Documentation has begun under recent discoveries. View both [DATA EXPUNGED] for more details. A note found on the back was also found, confirming SCP-4273 may indeed be sentient to a degree.</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;recovered&nbsp;advertisement</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Collapse&nbsp;recovered&nbsp;advertisement</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <blockquote> <p>Illegible. Text is covered by a sticker attached reading “Just in time for the holidays!”<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-800907-19" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >19</a></sup></p> <p>If so, you clearly have not purchased Arnex Convayance's newest line of combat transportation, the D.A.T! That stands for Defensive Assault Trucks people! Not only have we made another vehicle capable of wiping out your neighboring city, but this time it can fend for itself! Watch it fight on its own, tearing through anyone who isn’t its owner! Plus, as an added bonus, this time it can protect its driver!-</p> <p>Easy to use as 123!</p> <p>Simply insert the bonded key* and presto! You're ready to claim the roads as your own! Only one signature from one of our five head factories is all that is needed to get one for yourself!**</p> <p>Don’t Worry folks! We still have our other combat vehicles you just can’t seem to get enough of!</p> <p>Contact -███-████-████ for more details and get your very own!</p> <p>[A large image of SCP-4273 with all of its components armed is shown in the center of the poster. A small family of four are standing next to it, with the youngest hanging from the [REDACTED].</p> <p>-<span style="font-size:xx-small;">All forms and contracts must be signed completely and willingly. Renex Industries is not responsible for any accidents that occur when the product is improperly used. Do not use during the 25th of december.</span></p> <p>*<span style="font-size:xx-small;">If the key is lost/destroyed, contact ███-███-████ for a new one, or for repair. It is advised to stay away from the D.A.T. until representatives arrive.</span></p> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p>** <span style="font-size:xx-small;">Preferably the Vehicle and Transportation Division, although the Assault and Defense Division is also available, as is the Head Division. The Gear and Attire Division along with the Health and Medical Division are last resorts.</span></p> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p><span style="font-size:xx-small;">Jim, we have a problem.</span></p> <p><span style="font-size:xx-small;">You’re whole “Use anything similar to a horse” plan is about to get us all into some deep trouble.</span></p> <p><span style="font-size:xx-small;">I would not worry usually but unfortunately the boss is coming by to make sure we make the delivery on time. How do you plan on explaining to him why we started using reindeer instead of the mares?</span></p> <p><span style="font-size:xx-small;">I get trying to find a replacement for the mares is hard, but for god’s sake, we needed those reindeer for the jet sleds! Not this.</span></p> <p><span style="font-size:xx-small;">And before you start asking what the big deal is, it's that they won’t start up and act like they’re supposed to. Boss wants these things moving by christmas, but it seems they'll only move DURING christmas. We need them to be ALWAYS active, like an actual animal, not some once a year zombie.</span></p> <p><span style="font-size:xx-small;">I don’t know what he’ll think, but odds are once he finds out his rage will be much more desirable than the big boss, which is saying something.</span></p> <p><span style="font-size:xx-small;">Also, we lost the one with the glowing red hood ornament. He’s gonna be pissed once he finds out.</span></p> </blockquote> </div> </div> </div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-ash-krueger" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2341051&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608972648" alt="Dr Ash Krueger" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2341051)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-ash-krueger" >Dr Ash Krueger</a></span></p> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-800907-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. Personnel with Level 1 clearance are prohibited from coming into contact with SCP-4273.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-800907-2"><a href="javascript:;" >2</a>. Decoy building 98-C may be used for family/friend gatherings, to maintain moral and security.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-800907-3"><a href="javascript:;" >3</a>. Testing has shown the horsepower of SCP-4273 may very well be . SCP-4273 is composed of an unknown metallic material capable of generating and resisting extreme temperatures, the highest recorded being 7,092ºC.[[footnote]]The default amount of heat generated has been comparable to the earth’s core.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-800907-4"><a href="javascript:;" >4</a>. It is for this reason that SCP-4273 has a tesla coil docking station in the containment chamber.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-800907-5"><a href="javascript:;" >5</a>. It is for this reason a package of C4 is located within SCP-4273’s containment chamber in the form of a present.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-800907-6"><a href="javascript:;" >6</a>. See <strong>After-Incident-Report-4273-RC</strong> for more details.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-800907-7"><a href="javascript:;" >7</a>. This can also be caused by faulty maintenance.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-800907-8"><a href="javascript:;" >8</a>. <strong>See Addendum: 4273-A-R/R</strong>for more details.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-800907-9"><a href="javascript:;" >9</a>. Approximately two weeks after the event, Dr. ██████ attempted to activate SCP-4273 before [DATA EXPUNGED]. This was also the first time that SCP-4273 seemed to respond “flawlessly” to its driver</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-800907-10"><a href="javascript:;" >10</a>. ██████ was later confirmed to have been scheduled to perform with SCP-4273 before the attack</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-800907-11"><a href="javascript:;" >11</a>. accompanied by an image of what appears to show a snowflake pattern of construction tools and various weaponry, and an electrified hammer in the center.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-800907-12"><a href="javascript:;" >12</a>. see Document-4273-p-G.O.I-XX</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-800907-13"><a href="javascript:;" >13</a>. See <strong>Document 4273-T2-A</strong> for full information on tests conducted with trailers.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-800907-14"><a href="javascript:;" >14</a>. around the size of the fourth largest recorded domestic horse</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-800907-15"><a href="javascript:;" >15</a>. It is for this reason SCP-4273 has not been disassembled to examine.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-800907-16"><a href="javascript:;" >16</a>. It is currently unknown if the individual is the owner or an employee of the company.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-800907-17"><a href="javascript:;" >17</a>. At least 3/4ths of site-95 were completely eradicated.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-800907-18"><a href="javascript:;" >18</a>. Examination afterward showed Agent had suffered a mild concussion.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-800907-19"><a href="javascript:;" >19</a>. the placing of the sticker suggests it was added hastily.</div> </div> 
				 	]]>
